---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Try HVAC Boot Camp | How Air Conditioning Moves Heat"
  description="Try a short, phone-first HVAC Boot Camp lesson about how an air conditioner removes and moves heat."
>
  <div class="trial-page">
    <section class="trial-intro">
      <div class="trial-intro-inner">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Free lesson preview</p><h1>See how Boot Camp helps when a concept does not click.</h1><p>This short preview uses the opening Unit 1 concept. Work through it on your phone or computer—no account required.</p></div>
        <div class="trial-meta"><span>Unit 1 · Lesson 1</span><strong>What cooling really means</strong><small>Preview · about 3 minutes</small></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="trial-workspace">
      <article class="lesson-phone" aria-labelledby="lesson-title">
        <header class="lesson-phone-header">
          <div><span>Unit 1 · How air conditioning moves heat</span><strong>Lesson 1 preview</strong></div>
          <div class="lesson-progress"><span></span></div>
        </header>

        <div class="lesson-body">
          <p class="preview-kicker">One idea</p>
          <h2 id="lesson-title">An air conditioner cools a space by removing heat.</h2>
          <p class="lesson-lead">It absorbs unwanted heat indoors, carries it with the refrigerant, and releases it outdoors. It does not manufacture cold.</p>

          <div class="state-grid">
            <div><span class="heat-step" aria-hidden="true">1</span><strong>Warm air</strong><p>Indoor air reaches the colder evaporator coil.</p></div>
            <div><span class="heat-step" aria-hidden="true">2</span><strong>Heat moves</strong><p>Heat moves from the warmer air toward the colder coil and refrigerant.</p></div>
            <div><span class="heat-step" aria-hidden="true">3</span><strong>Cooler air</strong><p>The air leaves the coil with less heat.</p></div>
          </div>

          <div class="lesson-help" aria-labelledby="help-title">
            <p id="help-title">Choose the help you need</p>
            <div class="help-buttons">
              <button type="button" data-help="simple">Explain it simply</button>
              <button type="button" data-help="example">Give me an HVAC example</button>
              <button type="button" data-help="why">Why does this matter?</button>
            </div>
            <div class="help-response" data-response="simple" hidden><strong>A simpler way:</strong><p>Think of a refrigerator. It removes heat from inside and releases that heat into the room. Your air conditioner moves indoor heat outdoors in the same basic way.</p></div>
            <div class="help-response" data-response="example" hidden><strong>HVAC example:</strong><p>If return air is 78°F and the evaporator coil is 45°F, heat moves from the warmer air into the colder coil and refrigerant.</p></div>
            <div class="help-response" data-response="why" hidden><strong>Why technicians need this:</strong><p>Knowing where heat should move helps you understand what the indoor coil and refrigerant are supposed to do before you learn the complete refrigeration cycle.</p></div>
          </div>

          <form class="quick-check" data-quick-check>
            <fieldset>
              <legend><span>Quick check</span>The indoor air is warmer than the evaporator coil. Which way will heat move?</legend>
              <label><input type="radio" name="heat-check" value="coil-to-air" /> From the coil into the air</label>
              <label><input type="radio" name="heat-check" value="air-to-coil" /> From the air into the coil</label>
              <label><input type="radio" name="heat-check" value="none" /> Heat will not move</label>
            </fieldset>
            <button class="button button-dark" type="submit">Check my answer</button>
            <p class="check-feedback" data-check-feedback aria-live="polite"></p>
          </form>
        </div>
      </article>

      <aside class="trial-decision">
        <p class="eyebrow">What this preview demonstrates</p>
        <h2>Short content. Useful choices. Immediate feedback.</h2>
        <p>The complete Unit 1 pilot is still under review. This sample follows the current student-facing Unit 1 draft and shows the intended learning rhythm.</p>
        <ul class="plain-check-list"><li>One concept per page</li><li>HVAC examples instead of generic examples</li><li>Help without leaving the lesson</li><li>A quick check before moving on</li></ul>
        <div class="trial-next-card"><strong>Like the approach?</strong><p>Review the complete Boot Camp and decide whether the course fits your goal.</p><a class="button button-primary" href="/hvac-boot-camp/">Explore HVAC Boot Camp</a><a class="text-link-dark" href="/pricing/">See plans and pricing →</a></div>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section class="trial-footer-note">
      <p><strong>Development note:</strong> This preview uses scripted responses from the Unit 1 review draft. Live AI is not connected.</p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <script>
    const helpButtons = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-help]");
    const responses = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-response]");

    helpButtons.forEach((button) => {
      button.addEventListener("click", () => {
        const target = button.dataset.help;
        helpButtons.forEach((item) => item.setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(item === button)));
        responses.forEach((response) => {
          response.hidden = response.dataset.response !== target;
        });
      });
    });

    const form = document.querySelector<HTMLFormElement>("[data-quick-check]");
    const feedback = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-check-feedback]");

    form?.addEventListener("submit", (event) => {
      event.preventDefault();
      const answer = new FormData(form).get("heat-check");
      if (!feedback) return;

      if (!answer) {
        feedback.className = "check-feedback needs-answer";
        feedback.textContent = "Choose an answer first.";
      } else if (answer === "air-to-coil") {
        feedback.className = "check-feedback correct";
        feedback.textContent = "Correct. Heat moves from the warmer indoor air toward the colder coil.";
      } else {
        feedback.className = "check-feedback incorrect";
        feedback.textContent = "Look at which one is warmer. Heat naturally moves from warmer material toward cooler material. Try again.";
      }
    });
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
